# Per-deployment values and every secret. Copy to .env; never commit that.
#
# Two readers: the services, through python-dotenv, and scripts/install.sh,
# which sources it as shell. Keep it to plain KEY=VALUE lines so both agree —
# quote a value that contains spaces or a #.
#
# Everything here has a working default in config/config.yaml or in
# common/config.py — this file exists to name the knobs, not because the
# satellite needs it to boot. There is deliberately no YAML key for a secret.

# ── Broker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MQTT_BROKER=localhost
# MQTT_PORT=1883

# ── LoRa (Heltec V4 / Meshtastic over the PL011 UART) ────────────────────────
# 115200 is not optional: the Meshtastic Python library opens the port
# hard-coded at that rate.
# LORA_PORT=/dev/serial0
# LORA_BAUDRATE=115200
# If this and the ground station disagree, messages are transmitted and received
# perfectly and simply never meet — the hardest kind of radio fault to diagnose.
# LORA_CHANNEL_INDEX=1

# ── Dashboard ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the built interface from cubesat-groundstation is deployed. Created at
# boot by systemd-tmpfiles (config/tmpfiles.d/cubesat.conf); filled by
# scripts/deploy-dashboard.sh.
# CUBESAT_DASHBOARD_ROOT=/var/lib/cubesat/dashboard
# 80, so the address on the demo card and the EXPO sticker needs no port; the
# unit grants CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for it. On a laptop use something above 1024.
# DASHBOARD_PORT=80

# ── Access point for EXPO ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by scripts/install.sh, which creates one NetworkManager connection from
# them and reads this file to do so. Nothing reads them at runtime: HOSTD raises
# and lowers the connection by name and asks NetworkManager what is actually
# being broadcast. The password is a secret and this is the only place it may
# be written down — NetworkManager keeps it at 0600 afterwards. Without it the
# install step is skipped and EXPO reports an error until the connection exists.
# CUBESAT_AP_SSID=cubesat
# CUBESAT_AP_PASSWORD=
# CUBESAT_AP_ADDRESS=192.168.66.1/24
# CUBESAT_AP_CONNECTION=cubesat-ap
# CUBESAT_AP_INTERFACE=wlan0

# ── Recorder ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DHS_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Floor on how often one attitude sample is recorded. Costs SD-card writes, not
# I2C bus time — DHS holds no hardware.
# DHS_ATTITUDE_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC=1.0

# ── Sensors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v1 or v3. Unset means the UV index is withheld rather than guessed: two
# revisions read one raw register with formulas that disagree by a factor of
# forty. Set it once the board is identified and the index appears with no code
# change.
# CUBESAT_SEN0501_REVISION=v3

# ── Development, on anything that is not a Raspberry Pi ─────────────────────
# Two separate axes: the HAL's fake sensors, and HOSTD's no-op executor.
# Running the whole stack on a laptop needs both.
# CUBESAT_MOCK_HARDWARE=1
# CUBESAT_MOCK_HOST=1
# CUBESAT_DATA_DIR=./data
